The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ A ] S, the only object is A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] S B, the last object inside a code fence is still A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. Since A and B are different objects but the fenced object remains A, the answer stays unchanged.